.TH str_is 3
.SH NAME
str_is \- check if all characters in a string satisfy a predicate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "str.h"
.PP
.BI "int str_is(const char *" s ", int (*" pred ")(int));"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B str_is
tests whether all characters in the string
.I s
satisfy the predicate function
.IR pred .
It returns 1 if all characters satisfy the predicate (and the string is
non-empty), and 0 otherwise.